<title>USA: Alex. Brown approves 3-for-2 stock split.</title>
<headline>Alex. Brown approves 3-for-2 stock split.</headline>
<dateline>BALTIMORE</dateline>
<text>
<p>Investment bank Alex. Brown Inc. said its board of directors Wednesday approved a three-for-two split of the company's common stock, payable Jan. 15.</p>
<p>The stock split will increase the number of shares outstanding to about 24 million, it said.</p>
<p>Alex. Brown is a holding company whose principal subsidiary is Alex. Brown &amp; Sons Inc., the oldest investment banking firm in the United States.</p>
</text>
